 "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting path from 695 to 1495 exists under the 600-unit relay limit (only 2 nodes reachable), and crucially none exists even with unlimited waiting, despite 588 nodes being temporally reachable from 695 and both nodes lying within a shared 2-hop static neighbourhood of hubs. Node 1495's only inbound contact is a single event from 1517, which 695 also cannot temporally reach, sealing the sole entry point. Endpoint activity is sparse (5 and 4 events) relative to 7,526 window events, so high global volume and static connectivity are ruled out as explanations."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion: no cascade.**\n\nKey findings:\n- **\u0394\u2264600 constraint (step_01):** from 695 only **2 nodes** are temporally reachable in the whole window \u2014 1495 is not among them.\n- **Unconstrained control (step_02):** even with *no* waiting limit, 695 temporally reaches 588 nodes but still never 1495. So the failure is not caused by the 600-unit budget; it is a genuine time-ordering barrier.\n- **Bottleneck (steps 05, 07, 09):** 1495 has only one incoming partner, 1517, via a single event. 695 cannot temporally reach 1517 either (step_08), so the sole entry route into 1495 is closed.\n- **Static-connectivity confounder (steps 06, 11):** ignoring time, 695 and 1495 sit in a large 2-hop neighbourhood (via hubs 800/904/274/933/1531), i.e. a time-ignoring path plausibly exists \u2014 yet no time-respecting one does.\n- **Volume/popularity confounders (steps 03, 10, 12, 13):** both endpoints are low-degree (5 and 4 events) in a window with 7,526 events and 1,954 active nodes; their joint activity is sparse and back-loaded (most events in the 56825\u201366424 bins), so the dense global activity cannot be mistaken for endpoint-specific cascade support. Reverse direction also fails (step_14).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_636b848d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [695, 1495, 1517],\n  \"window\": [28025, 66424],\n  \"confidence\": 0.92,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting path from 695 to 1495 exists under the 600-unit relay limit (only 2 nodes reachable), and crucially none exists even with unlimited waiting, despite 588 nodes being temporally reachable from 695 and both nodes lying within a shared 2-hop static neighbourhood of hubs. Node 1495's only inbound contact is a single event from 1517, which 695 also cannot temporally reach, sealing the sole entry point. Endpoint activity is sparse (5 and 4 events) relative to 7,526 window events, so high global volume and static connectivity are ruled out as explanations.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 48239, "total_output_tokens": 3656, "total_tokens": 51895, "total_latency_ms": 53316, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}